The community-nodes work in the tree referenced three files that were never
created, so `quasar build` failed:

  src/stores/community-nodes    (imported by GalaxyPage.vue, SurfaceViewPage.vue)
  src/pages/CommunityNodesPage.vue  (imported by routes.ts)
  src/pages/AdminNodesPage.vue      (imported by routes.ts)

Adds deliberate stubs so the build passes, and the spec DOCS.md already links to.

fetchGalleryNodes() returns an empty list rather than querying the
`community_nodes` table, which has no migration and does not exist. That
reproduces the pre-feature behaviour exactly — systems show no galleries — so
nothing renders differently. The signature matches both call sites and is the
one contract a real implementation must keep.

SPEC_COMMUNITY_NODES.md documents the table, the mapping to OrbitalGalleryEntry,
node_type extensibility without migrations, and the access-control posture
inherited from migration 007 (clients never assert their own trust decisions;
moderation goes through a SECURITY DEFINER RPC with search_path pinned). It
records five open questions for review — the blocking one being where the admin
role comes from, since /admin/community-nodes is not access-controlled today.

Note: DOCS.md also links SETTLEMENT_ADDRESS_API.md and
blog-settlement-address-api.md, which likewise do not exist. Not addressed here.

Verified: `quasar build` exits 0; both stub routes render; vue-tsc drops from
342 to 338 errors (the two missing-module errors in routes.ts are resolved) with
zero errors in the new files; eslint clean.

