+# Exotopia Community Nodes — Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1 (draft)
+**Date:** 2026-07-31
+**Status:** Specced — not implemented; stubs in tree
+
+---
+
+## Purpose
+
+Community nodes are the member-authored entries that populate a star system's
+orbital gallery: business listings and locations, creative pages, and node types
+not yet defined. They are the first thing to fill the `OrbitalGalleryEntry`
+pipeline, which has been rendered by `DefenderNav.vue` but never fed by real data.
+
+Three audiences:
+- **Members** — publish a listing or creative page tied to a place in the map
+- **Visitors** — see what exists around a system when they arrive
+- **Operators** — moderate submissions before they appear publicly
+
+---
+
+## Current state (what exists in the tree today)
+
+This spec was written against a set of deliberate stubs, added so the app builds
+while the feature is designed. Three call sites already exist and must keep working:
+
+| File | Expects |
+|---|---|
+| `src/stores/community-nodes.ts` | **stub** — `useCommunityNodesStore()` with `fetchGalleryNodes(hostname): Promise<OrbitalGalleryEntry[]>`, currently returns `[]` |
+| `src/pages/GalaxyPage.vue:1526` | `fetchGalleryNodes(sys.hostname)`, guards against a slow fetch resolving after navigation |
+| `src/pages/SurfaceViewPage.vue:2906` | `fetchGalleryNodes(system?.hostname ?? null)` |
+| `src/pages/CommunityNodesPage.vue` | **stub** — member-facing `/my-listings` |
+| `src/pages/AdminNodesPage.vue` | **stub** — `/admin/community-nodes` moderation |
+| `src/stores/member.ts:180` | already exports `community_nodes` rows filtered by `owner_id` — **the table does not exist yet**, so this export row is currently dead |
+
+The stubs return empty rather than querying a missing table, which reproduces the
+pre-feature behaviour exactly: systems show no galleries, nothing renders differently.
+
+**Also dangling:** `DOCS.md` references `SETTLEMENT_ADDRESS_API.md` and
+`blog-settlement-address-api.md`, neither of which exists. Unrelated to this spec,
+but they are broken links in the same doc table.
+
+---
+
+## Data model
+
+### `community_nodes`
+
+```sql
+create table public.community_nodes (
+  id             uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
+  owner_id       uuid not null references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,
+  node_type      text not null,              -- see extensibility below
+  name           text not null,
+  description    text,
+  hostname       text not null,              -- host star; the gallery query key
+  status         text not null default 'draft',
+                 -- draft | submitted | approved | rejected | withdrawn
+  -- Orbit placement (maps to GalleryOrbitAnchor)
+  anchor_type    text not null default 'free',   -- free | lagrange | circumbinary
+  radius_au      numeric,
+  initial_angle_deg numeric,
+  anchor_planet  text,                       -- lagrange only
+  lagrange_point text,                        -- 'L4' | 'L5'
+  -- Presentation
+  gallery_type   text not null default 'community',  -- GalleryType
+  ownership_model text not null default 'solo',      -- GalleryOwnershipModel
+  access_level   text not null default 'public',     -- GalleryAccessLevel
+  pon_ink_url    text,
+  created_at     timestamptz not null default now(),
+  updated_at     timestamptz not null default now()
+);
+
+create index on public.community_nodes (hostname) where status = 'approved';
+create index on public.community_nodes (owner_id);
+```
+
+`hostname` is the query key because both call sites fetch by host star. It must be
+a bare NASA-archive designation — apply the same `assertBareField` discipline used
+in `src/lib/settlements.ts` so a hostname can never smuggle a delimiter.
+
+### Mapping to `OrbitalGalleryEntry`
+
+The store maps rows to the existing interface in `src/lib/defender-nav.types.ts`.
+Do **not** widen that interface for storage concerns — it is a render contract.
+
+| `OrbitalGalleryEntry` field | Source |
+|---|---|
+| `id`, `name` | column |
+| `galleryType`, `ownershipModel`, `accessLevel` | column |
+| `orbitAnchor` | assembled from `anchor_type` + the anchor columns into the discriminated union |
+| `radiusAU` | `radius_au`, or derived for `lagrange` from the anchor planet's orbit |
+| `currentAngleDeg` | **not stored** — initialised from `initial_angle_deg`, then updated per frame by the parent |
+| `meetingState` | `'idle'` until live meetings exist (see Deferred) |
+| `presenceCount` | `0` until presence exists (see Deferred) |
+| `scheduledEvent` | null until events exist |
+| `skyAzimuth` / `skyAltitude` | set by `SurfaceViewPage` when projected into `skyObjects`, not by the store |
+
+---
+
+## `node_type` extensibility
+
+`node_type` is a free-text column validated against a catalogue in code, not a
+Postgres enum — adding a type must not require a migration.
+
+- Catalogue lives in `src/data/community-node-types.ts` as
+  `Record<string, { label, description, galleryTypeDefault, fields }>`.
+- Unknown `node_type` values read from the DB render with a generic presentation
+  rather than throwing — a client on an older bundle must not break when a newer
+  type appears.
+- Validation on write is against the catalogue; validation on read is permissive.
+
+Starter types: `business_listing`, `location`, `creative_page`.
+
+---
+
+## Access control
+
+The reward-ledger hardening in `supabase/migrations/007_reward_integrity.sql`
+established the posture this feature must follow: **clients do not get to assert
+their own trust decisions.**
+
+- RLS on: owner can `select`/`insert`/`update` their own rows in `draft`/`submitted`.
+- Public `select` restricted to `status = 'approved'` only.
+- **Clients may never set `status` to `approved`.** Moderation transitions go
+  through a `SECURITY DEFINER` RPC with `search_path` pinned to `public, pg_temp`,
+  matching the pattern in migration 007.
+- `/admin/community-nodes` is **not** access-controlled by the router today. The
+  admin page must gate on a server-checked role; an unlisted route is not a control.
+  Decide the role source (a `profiles.role` column, or a dedicated `admins` table)
+  before building the page — this is the main open question below.
+
+---
+
+## Privacy and export
+
+`src/stores/member.ts` already lists `community_nodes` in the per-member data
+export, filtered by `owner_id`. Once the table exists that row starts returning
+data with no further change — confirm the export includes only the owner's rows and
+no moderation metadata about other members.
+
+Self-host / export story: a member's nodes should be exportable as a portable JSON
+document that a self-hosted instance can import, so a listing is not locked to this
+deployment. Define the envelope alongside the first implementation, not after.
+
+---
+
+## Deferred (explicitly not in a first pass)
+
+These fields exist on `OrbitalGalleryEntry` and must be populated with inert
+defaults rather than designed now:
+
+- **Live meetings** (`meetingState` beyond `'idle'`) — needs a realtime channel
+- **Presence** (`presenceCount`) — needs the same
+- **Scheduled events** (`scheduledEvent`) — needs a scheduling model and timezone story
+- **Ticketed access** (`accessLevel: 'ticket'`) — do not build; it implies payments,
+  which this repo has deliberately kept out (see `RISK_REDUCTION_RECOMMENDATIONS.md`
+  and the Exchange Depot removal). Leave the enum value unused.
+
+---
+
+## Open questions for review
+
+1. **Admin role source** — where does "is this user a moderator" come from? Nothing
+   in the schema answers this today. Blocks `AdminNodesPage.vue`.
+2. **Placement conflicts** — two nodes can claim the same radius/angle around one
+   host. Fail on write, or let them overlap visually?
+3. **Per-host cap** — should one system limit how many approved nodes it shows,
+   for both render cost and squatting?
+4. **Moderation SLA** — does a `submitted` node auto-expire if unreviewed?
+5. **Hostname validity** — must `hostname` resolve to a known system in the galaxy
+   dataset at write time, or can a node point at a not-yet-catalogued host?
+
+---
+
+## Implementation checklist
+
+1. Migration: table, indexes, RLS policies, moderation RPC (`search_path` pinned).
+2. `src/data/community-node-types.ts` — type catalogue.
+3. Replace the body of `fetchGalleryNodes()` in `src/stores/community-nodes.ts`;
+   keep the signature — both call sites depend on it.
+4. Build out `CommunityNodesPage.vue` (owner CRUD) and `AdminNodesPage.vue`
+   (moderation, behind the role gate from Q1).
+5. Verify the `member.ts` export row now returns owner-scoped rows.
+6. Add `SPEC_COMMUNITY_NODES.md` status → Active in `DOCS.md` once shipped.
